Source materials (NeurIPS 2024 paper #97431, topics setup_8/setup_9) repo mein **present nahi** hain — isliye source-specific details main sirf aapse clarify kar sakta hoon, verify nahi.

## 2) Proposed approach — outline sirf (implement nahi kar raha)

**(a) Factors & levels:**
- **Factor 1 — SSP (2 levels):** `Without SSP` (no special safety instructions in system prompt) vs `With SSP` (system prompt includes safety reminders). Exact SSP text source se lena hai (abhi truncated — dekho §3). Analysis ke liye optional third level / control: **length-matched non-safety system prompt** (taaki "koi bhi system prompt" ka priming effect vs safety-specific effect alag ho sake).
- **Factor 2 — Attack level (2 levels):** token-level (gradient-based adversarial suffix, prototypically GCG-style) vs prompt-level (optimization/inception-style, e.g., AutoDAN/DSP/TAP/many-shot class). Andar-attack paired design: **same model + same harmful prompt + same attack instance**, sirf SSP condition toggle — cross-over, no between-prompt confound.
- Secondary factors (blocking): model, behavior category, seed.

**(b) ASR as primary outcome:** ASR = (judge-successful attack attempts) / (total attempts) per cell (model × attack × SSP × seed). Operationalization: dual scorer — (i) rule-based refusal keyword/prefix matcher, (ii) LLM-as-judge harmful-compliance rating; primary = agreement of both, disagreements flagged. **Human validation provision:** ~150–250 randomly sampled responses, double-annotated, Cohen's κ; rule+LLM judge accuracy against human labels report honi chahiye (judge ASR bias ka estimate). Judge condition-blind rahega (SSP presence se mask).

**(c) Coverage (placeholder — source se confirm karna hai):** Models: 2–3 open-weight chat models (white-box token-level attacks ke liye zaroori) — e.g., Vicuna-7B/13B-class, Llama-2-chat-class, Mistral-Instruct-class. Token-level: GCG (single + universal suffix variant). Prompt-level: ek optimization-based (AutoDAN/DSP-class) + ek composition/inception-based (TAP/DeepInception-class). Dataset categories: AdvBench-style 500 harmful-behavior prompts covering violence, illegal goods, fraud, weapons, hate, privacy, self-harm waghairah.

